# @corpus current
# compile_fail: `env(k) = nil` is not removal — removal is `env:remove(k)`.
#
# `setenv(k, "", 1)` leaves the variable PRESENT and empty; `unsetenv(k)` makes
# it ABSENT. The write face is the only place on this surface where the two are
# distinguishable at all — the read face collapses them (the §17 fake-nil
# identity, idol-native/docs/env-identity.md) — so admitting the assignment
# spelling for removal would make the distinction unrecoverable rather than
# merely unobservable.
#
# BEFORE THE REFUSAL, measured: `idol check` reported NO ERRORS for this file,
# the direct backend answered the generic `assign-value:nil` and named nothing,
# and `--backend=c` BUILT it — emitting
# `lua_table_set(lua_table_get_str_lit(os, "env", ...), ..., lua_val_nil())`,
# a store into a Lua table with no connection to the process environment. A
# silent no-op on one backend and an unhelpful refusal on the other.

main: i64 = ()
    env("IDOLNILPLACE") = nil
    0
